blocks.en:
Generative AI models directly address these challenges by capturing the underlying probability distribution of medical imaging data and enabling synthesis of new, anatomically plausible samples. They offer a plethora of applications in medical imaging:
(a) Generation of artificial but anatomically plausible new images, which are free from privacy concerns and can be used to train other DL models;
(b) Conditional image generation based on patient characteristics (e.g. age, disease), segmentation masks, or text (e.g. radiology reports);
(c) Image augmentation (e.g. denoising, upsampling, artifact correction) or domain transfer (e.g. T1 → \rightarrow T2 MRI, MRI → \rightarrow CT);
(d) Reconstruction (e.g. low-field MRI, sparse-view CBCT, low-dose PET);
(e) Inpainting, e.g. of artificial tumors into images of healthy subjects, to address data scarcity or class imbalance.

blocks.zh:
基因AI模型通过捕捉医学成像数据的基本概率分布和对新的、解剖学上可行的样品进行合成,直接应对这些挑战。 它们为医疗成像提供了大量应用:
(a) 制作人造但解剖上可信的新图像,这些图像不涉及隐私问题,可用于培训其他DL模型;
(b) 根据病人的特征(如年龄、疾病)、分裂口罩或文字(如放射报告)生成有条件的图像;
(c) 图像扩增(例如去诺氏,升标,文物校正)或域转移(例如T1 → 右旋T2磁共振,MRI → 右旋CT);
(d) 重建(例如低地磁共振、低视差CBCT、低剂量PET);
(e) 将人工肿瘤涂成健康主体的图像,以解决数据稀缺或阶级失衡问题。

blocks.en:
Reducing the GPU memory footprint of large 3D generative models is an active concern shared by GAN- and
diffusion-based architectures alike, addressed by several general-purpose techniques including:
(i) Gradient checkpointing, which trades additional compute for memory by discarding and recomputing intermediate activations during the backward pass instead of storing all of them [ 106 ] ;
(ii) Mixed-precision training, which reduces the memory of weights, gradients and activations by computing in half precision wherever numerically safe [ 107 ] ;
(iii) Memory-efficient and linear-complexity attention, avoiding materializing the full 𝒪 ⁡ ( n 2 ) \mathcal{O}(n^{2}) attention matrix in transformer-based models [ 108 , 64 ] ;
(iv) Model and tensor parallelism, which distribute a single model’s weights and activations across multiple GPUs, rather than reducing the footprint on any one device [ 109 , 110 ] .

blocks.zh:
减少大型3D基因模型的GPU内存足迹是GAN和GAN共同关切的一个积极因素。
以传播为基础的结构,包括下列几种通用技术:
(一) 渐进式检查,通过在后行通行证期间丢弃和重置中间激活器,而不是储存所有中间激活器来进行额外的内存计算[106];
(二) 混合精度训练,在数字安全的地方,通过半精度计算减少重量、梯度和激活的内存[107];
(三) 内存高效和线性复杂注意,避免在变压器型号中实现完整的O ⁡(n 2)\mathcal{O}(n^{2})注意矩阵[108,64];
(四)模型和拉力平行主义,它将单一模型的重量和激活量分布在多个GPU之间,而不是减少任何一种设备上的足迹[109,110].

blocks.en:
Some of the best performing 3D GAN based approaches, which are also used as benchmarks for the DMs presented in section 7 , are:
3D-alpha-WGAN [ 112 ] , which combines VAE and GAN using an additional code discriminator network, coupled with WGAN-GP to generate brain MRIs in full 3D;
CCE-GAN [ 113 ] , which builds upon 3D-alpha-WGAN, but employs the Wasserstein loss explicitly in the latent space and uses cycle consistency;
HA-GAN [ 114 ] , which uses a hierarchical training scheme with a low-resolution volume and high-resolution sub-volumes to generate brain MRI and thorax CT images.

blocks.zh:
以3D GAN为基础的一些绩效最好的方法,这些方法也被用作第7节提出的模式草案的基准:
3D-alpha-WGAN [112],结合VAE和GAN,使用额外的代码歧义网络,加之WGAN-GP,在全3D中生成大脑MRI;
CCE-GAN [113],它以3D-α-WGAN为基础,但在潜在空间中明确使用瓦瑟斯坦损失,并使用周期一致性;
HA-GAN [114],它使用分级的训练计划,具有低分辨率的体积和高分辨率的子体积生成脑磁共振和胸腔CT图像.
